Z||000000||Ozzy||11-03-1999||08:53 PM||||I have a chance to buy a '91 2.5l duck that has been modified fairly extensively. Forged pistons, steel crank, able to leap tall buildings in a single bound etc, etc!<P>Can I fit this engine to my '88 Coupe easily...Hang on, Nuthin' is really easy with the Fiero! (Whut am I thinking???) I should say with a minimum of fuss.<P>This engine was reportedly built for the track (modified stock or sumthin' like that)and will supposedly produce 175HP. It is a new rebuild and has been stashed away in this mechanics shop while he waits for the right rig to throw it in. He is starting a new bussiness though, so I can get it for around $900.00. My Duke also has a new rebuild on it and I could sell it to offset the cost a little.<P>Any thoughts would be appreciated.<P>Curious Ozzy||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||11-03-1999||10:58 PM||||without knowing what changes they made, especially to the EFI, and DIS, there's no real way to know.<P>Assuming the starter, waterpump, and other things are right, it may fit. may. If they changed the EFI and/or DIS then you could have problems ECM wise depending on what they did.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ozzy||11-03-1999||11:58 PM||||Hey there Ogre... Hey cool web site by the way!<P>Yeah, I asked the obvious like...Distributor or DIS (especially as I have recently become well aquainted with the ubiquitous DIS system) He tells me that he thinks the crank sensor port is there and that I could plug the distributor port. Also that it is a serpentine setup. I guess how far forward the water pump extends as well as the self tensioner mounting etc would be issues. <P>I thought I read somewhere in another post that transfering from a rear wheel drive to a transverse mounting that the starter motor had some kind of problem. <P>What about the bolt up to the transmission? (5 speed) Where there any major changes to the block on this engine from '88 to '91?<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
